## Modular Directory & Package Layout

Organize code by **feature**, then separate each feature into data, domain, and presentation packages. Keep shared infrastructure in `core`.

The tree below shows a package layout within one Gradle module. Packages provide organization; separate Gradle modules and dependency rules are needed to enforce build-time boundaries. When splitting modules, presentation and data depend on domain, and the application composition root wires the implementations.

```text
app/src/main/java/com/enterprise/mobile/
├── core/                                   # Shared enterprise infrastructure
│   ├── database/                           # Room database configuration & migrations
│   ├── network/                            # Retrofit, OkHttp clients & auth interceptors
│   ├── security/                           # Approved credential storage & Keystore integration
│   └── ui/theme/                           # Enterprise design tokens (Color, Type, Shape)
│
├── di/                                     # Global singleton dependency injection
│   ├── AppModule.kt                        # Application-scoped providers
│   ├── NetworkModule.kt                    # Authenticated OkHttp & Retrofit providers
│   └── DatabaseModule.kt                   # Room DB & DAO providers
│
└── feature/user/                           # USER FEATURE PACKAGES
    ├── data/                               # Data Layer: Single Source of Truth
    │   ├── remote/
    │   │   ├── dto/UserNetworkDto.kt       # API serialization model
    │   │   └── UserApiService.kt           # Retrofit endpoint definition
    │   ├── local/
    │   │   ├── entity/UserEntity.kt        # Room database entity
    │   │   └── dao/UserDao.kt              # Room DAO with SQLite queries
    │   ├── mapper/UserMappers.kt           # DTO -> Entity -> Domain mappings
    │   └── repository/UserRepositoryImpl.kt # Repository implementation (Observe + Refresh)
    │
    ├── domain/                             # Pure Domain Layer: Zero Android Framework APIs
    │   ├── model/UserDomainModel.kt        # Immutable Kotlin business model
    │   ├── repository/UserRepository.kt    # Repository interface (boundary contract)
    │   └── usecase/GetUserProfileUseCase.kt # Single-purpose business use case
    │
    ├── di/                                 # Feature bindings installed in application scope
    │   └── UserFeatureModule.kt            # Binds repository interfaces to implementations
    │
    └── presentation/                       # UI Layer: Jetpack Compose + ViewModels
        ├── state/
        │   ├── UserProfileUiState.kt       # Immutable screen state
        │   └── UserProfileUiEvent.kt       # Screen actions
        ├── UserProfileViewModel.kt         # Hilt-injected ViewModel (StateFlow producer)
